>>
Rule 1 (input and values tensors must have the same dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 2 (axis must be within valid range for arr, supporting negative indexing)
{v_1 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= (0 - ndim(v_1)) ≤ v_3 ∧ v_3 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 4 (non-axis dimensions must match when axis is provided; negative axis is normalized)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if i = (if v_3 < 0 then v_3 + ndim(v_1) else v_3) then true else shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 6 (axis must also be within the valid range for values)
{v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= (0 - ndim(v_2)) ≤ v_3 ∧ v_3 ≤ ndim(v_2) - 1
>>
Rule 7 (dtype meta-type is not allowed for tensor elements)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 12 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 12
